# Milestone: v0.13.3 (refactor-3 SCHED-05 spec-review hazard 1)
# Covers: tag.stop() fired from an AT_SYNC inline body — i.e. from INSIDE
#         watcher_eval_dirty's active-list walk — retiring a waituntil
#         member's watcher must NOT pool_free it mid-walk: the walk's
#         captured `next` pointer is the waituntil watcher (installed
#         immediately after the at-sync watcher, so it IS the snapshot —
#         ordering assumption this fixture depends on), and a freed slot's
#         next_active is repurposed as the pool freelist link.
#         Pre-fix: the walk continued into the freed slot and then into the
#         freelist (mode 0 slots) — "unknown watcher mode" assert abort in
#         checked builds; silent freelist-slot writes in release builds.
#         Post-fix: mid-eval the unpark WATCHER arm scrubs waiter_strand and
#         defers the retire via pending_onleave_queue_push (PENDING_UNREGISTER
#         keeps the snapshot valid; the pool_free happens at the next
#         safepoint drain).  The woken strand's tail is straight-line, so the
#         deposit drops (v0.13.1-G) and the full body runs: log == "WA".
#         The trailing Realm.nop() call provides the dispatch safepoint that
#         drains the deferred entry (the pending-onleave drain runs at
#         safepoints only until Task 5's idle pump), so the final step
#         reports QUIESCENT.
# matrix-row: tag-stop
## timeout: 30
## host: run var t = Tag.new()
## host: run Realm.flag = 0
## host: run Realm.go = 0
## host: run Realm.log = ""
## host: run at sync (Realm.go == 1) { Realm.t.stop() }
## host: run t: { waituntil(Realm.flag == 1); Realm.log = Realm.log + "W" }; Realm.log = Realm.log + "A"
## host: run var trig = function() { Realm.go = 1 }; Realm.trig()
## host: run Realm.log
## host: run var nop = function() { 0 }; Realm.nop()
## host: step 1000
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] ""
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 1
[00000000] "WA"
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
